.TH CRUNCH_SYSFS 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
crunch_sysfs \- invokes the obsolete linux sysfs syscall with raw arguments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/legacy_syscalls.h>
.B long crunch_sysfs(int option, unsigned long argument1, unsigned long argument2);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes the obsolete Linux sysfs syscall with raw integer arguments. Use
.BR crunch_sysfs_index (3crunch)
and
.BR crunch_sysfs_name (3crunch)
for operations requiring pointers. Availability and permissions depend on the kernel.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysfs (2)
